WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
[speaking Minionese]

2
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
[screams]

3
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
[chuckles]
[Bob sighs]

4
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.000
[electricity hums]

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Ah. Hmm.

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.000
[screams]
[exclaims]

7
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.000
[chuckles] Stuart.

8
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Illumination! [laughs]

9
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
["Double Life" playing]

10
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.000
♪ That's the question ♪

11
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.000
♪ Who will Gru be tonight? ♪

12
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
♪ That's the question ♪

13
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.000
♪ Hey, what are you hiding? ♪

14
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
♪ Whatcha doing
When you gone? ♪

15
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.000
♪ Nothing wrong being private ♪

16
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.000
♪ Make sure it ain't wrong ♪

17
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
♪ Your life, double-sided ♪

18
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
♪ Two-faced like coins ♪

19
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.000
♪ What side do I get? ♪

20
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.000
♪ Which side are you on? ♪

21
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.000
♪ So what have you done? ♪

22
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.000
♪ Some of your dirt
Has come to light ♪

23
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.000
♪ Why were you ♪

24
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
♪ Speeding up that hill
Until the brakes came off? ♪

25
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
♪ And someone saw you
In a fight ♪

26
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.000
♪ Am I right? ♪

27
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
♪ I know
You heard the rumors ♪

28
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.000
♪ You must get over to it
Right away ♪

29
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.000
♪ If anyone can do it ♪

30
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.000
♪ You gotta get there soon ♪

31
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.000
♪ It's not okay ♪

32
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.000
♪ You got cars to drive ♪

33
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
♪ Plenty jets to fly ♪

34
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
♪ When will you arrive? ♪

35
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.000
♪ You're running out of time ♪

36
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.000
♪ Don't you see that everything
Is on the line? ♪

37
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
♪ Am I right? ♪

38
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.000
♪ Who will you be tonight? ♪

39
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.000
♪ That's the question ♪

40
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.000
♪ Who will Gru be tonight? ♪

41
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.000
♪ That's the question ♪

42
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.000
♪ The thrill
Of the double life ♪

43
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
-[car alarm chirps]
-[tires screech]

44
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
[grunting]

45
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
[laughs]

46
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Phil, Ron, Ralph! Stay focused.

47
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.000
Uh. Uh, okay, okay.

48
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.000
[Ralph] Hmm.

49
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Okay, our target
is Maxime Le Mal,

50
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.000
one of the Anti-Villain League's
most wanted.

51
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.000
And, trust me, a real jerk.

52
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.000
So, there is no room
for error. Got it?

53
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Sí, boss.

54
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.000
[inhales]

55
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.000
[speaking Minionese]

56
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.000
["Word Up" playing]

57
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.000
Phil, Ron!

58
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.000
[speaking Minionese, laughs]

59
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.000
[speaking Minionese]

60
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.000
[exclaims]

61
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.000
[speaking Minionese] Ah.

62
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.000
[grunting]
Ah!

63
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.000
[speaking Minionese, muffled]

64
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.000
[person] Kids can be so cruel,
but Maxime can be even crueler.

65
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000
[laughing]

66
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.000
Ho, ho, ho.
Well, well, well.

67
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.000
Look who it is.

68
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.000
If it isn't Gru-ser the Loser.

69
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.000
Well, if it isn't Maxime Le Mal.
You look--

70
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Magnificent? Yes, I know.

71
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.000
What did you think, huh?

72
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
I was going to look
like a bald loser
with a dad bod?

73
00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Oops. Looks like
you beat me to it, no?

74
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.000
[crowd murmuring, gasping]

75
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.000
Ooh.
Ooh!

76
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Oh.

77
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.000
It's good to laugh, no?

78
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.000
[chuckles]

79
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Anyway, you remember
my girlfriend, Valentina?

80
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.000
She was captain of
the Femme Fatale cheer squad,

81
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.000
and the most popular girl
at school, huh?

82
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.000
I remember.

83
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Good to see you, Valentina.

84
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.000
[scoffs]
[dog growls]

85
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.000
[chuckles] What happened, Gru?

86
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:34.000
All your dreams of becoming
a famous villain,
they go poof-poof, huh?

87
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.000
Well, I don't know if you know,

88
00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.000
but I did manage
to steal the moon.

89
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Really?

90
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.000
You mean, that moon?

91
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.000
[laughs]

92
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.000
[feedback whines]
[principal] Is this on?

93
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Can I have
everyone's attention, please?

94
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Good evening and welcome,
Lycée Pas Bon alumni.

95
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Now, we're going to
kick off the festivities

96
00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.000
by announcing the winner
of our most coveted award,

97
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.000
The Golden Alumni.

98
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.000
[crowd cheers]

99
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.000
And so, without further ado,

100
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:13.000
the winner of this year's
Golden Alumni is, uh...

101
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.000
Oh, my favorite student.

102
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Maxime Le Mal.

103
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.000
What?
Are you kidding me?
Thank you. Thank you.

104
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.000
Merci. Merci beaucoup.

105
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.000
No, you don't have to.

106
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.000
[groans]

107
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.000
["Unbelievable" plays]

108
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.000
[laughs]

109
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Oh, thank you. Thank you.

110
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.000
Thank you.

111
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.000
I'm sure you all know

112
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.000
that I have something
very big in the works.

113
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:43.000
Now, some of you laughed at
my childhood obsession
with cockroaches.

114
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.000
But I quickly learned
that they are
a miracle of evolution.

115
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
[crowd murmuring]

116
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.000
And I have found a way
to harness the strength

117
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.000
and the speed and the--
What is the word?

118
00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.000
"Unsquishability" of the most
powerful creature on the planet.

119
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:06.000
Which makes me
indestructible and unstoppable!

120
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.000
Maxime! Maxime! Maxime!

121
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.000
Behold the power
of the cockroach!

122
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.000
[grunts]

123
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.000
[crowd gasping]

124
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.000
[gasps]

125
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.000
[Maxime laughs]

126
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.000
[imitating Maxime]

127
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.000
[exclaiming, speaking Minionese]

128
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.000
So, my sad little friend,
what do you say about that, huh?

129
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.000
Well, I'd say you're...

130
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:53.000
under arrest,
courtesy of
the Anti-Villain League.

131
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.000
Oh... [chuckles]
...I don't think so, mon ami.

132
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.000
Oh, yeah? Goop grenade!

133
00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
[yelps]

134
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.000
[grunts]

135
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.000
No!

136
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.000
[chuckles] Hi-yah!

137
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Move in.

138
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.000
[agent 1] AVL!
[agent 2] Everybody, freeze!

139
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.000
-[agent 3] Stay where you are.
-[agent 4] Move!

140
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.000
Ha!

141
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.000
[agent 5] Stay there!

142
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.000
Freeze!

143
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.000
Gotcha!

144
00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.000
No, no, no! No!

145
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.000
This is not happening!

146
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.000
C'est impossible. [grunts]

147
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.000
Get your hands off of me!

148
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.000
-I am commanding you
to let me go.
-[chuckles]

149
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.000
So long, Maxime!

150
00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.000
Who's the loser now?

151
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.000
[both] Loser, loser, loser!

152
00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.000
[Maxime screams]

153
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.000
This is not over!

154
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.000
You won't always
have the AVL

155
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.000
to fight your battles,
you coward!

156
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.000
Mark my words!
I will exterminate you!

157
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.000
[laughing]

158
00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.000
[chuckles] Not, uh--
Not scary at all. [chuckles]

159
00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.000
[birds chirping]

160
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.000
[Lucky bleats]

161
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.000
Hello, everybody!

162
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.000
[Edith] Gru, what's up?
[Agnes] Yay, Gru!

163
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.000
Hey, Gru.
I'm so happy
you're here!

164
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.000
What's shaking
in the Gru house?

165
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.000
Look what I taught Lucky.

166
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.000
-Lucky, sit.
-[bleats]

167
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.000
[farts, bleats]

168
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:56.000
Aw, Lucky, I said sit.

169
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.000
[bleats]
[giggles]

170
00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.000
Well, it is only
his first lesson.

171
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.000
Uh, maybe we practice
outside from now on.

172
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.000
There's my favorite husband!

173
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Did you remember
to get the milk?

174
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.000
Well, yes. They had a few kinds.

175
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.000
They got the almond milk,
soy milk, hemp milk,

176
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.000
oat milk, goat milk,
chocolate milk, half-and-half,

177
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.000
powdered, and of magnesia.

178
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.000
What about regular milk?

179
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
No, they don't
make that anymore.

180
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.000
Oh!

181
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.000
Wait a minute.

182
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.000
[Agnes giggles]
One, two, three girls.

183
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.000
One wife.

184
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.000
Something is missing.
[children giggle]

185
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.000
No, I think
that's all of us. Yeah.

186
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.000
You know what?
I keep forgetting...

187
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.000
this guy!
[gurgles]

188
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.000
Oh, ho, ho! There's my boy!

189
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.000
There he is!

190
00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Ah, coochy, coochy, coochy.

191
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.000
Where is Daddy's hug? [gasps]

192
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Oh, looks like
somebody's a little cranky!

193
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.000
Behind that sourpuss,
I know you love your dada!

194
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.000
Go on, say it.

195
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.000
Dada. Dada.

196
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Yes, of course
he loves you! He just--
[babbles]

197
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.000
He just doesn't show it
on his face,

198
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.000
or with his body language.

199
00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.000
Right, Gru Jr? Come on.

200
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.000
Show Daddy how much
you love him.

201
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.000
Oh, I know what
will make you happy!

202
00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.000
Mmm, Bahama Medley!

203
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.000
[cries]

204
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:25.000
No? It's from The Bahamas.

205
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.000
All of them. Look.

206
00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:30.000
Oh, so yummy!

207
00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.000
Mmm, mmm, mmm.

208
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.000
[coughs, gags]

209
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.000
Oh, that really tastes
like The Bahamas!

210
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.000
See? He loves his daddy!

211
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.000
He's sharing. [chuckles]

212
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.000
[laughing]

213
00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.000
Phil, Ralph, Ron!

214
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.000
["Hot for Teacher" plays]
Hup, hup, hup!

215
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.000
Hup!

216
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.000
Pistachio. Yeah, cashew.

217
00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.000
[giggles]

218
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.000
[speaking Minionese]

219
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.000
Gotcha!

220
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.000
[speaking Minionese]

221
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.000
[speaking Minionese]

222
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:08.000
[speaking Minionese]

223
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.000
Thanks, guys.

224
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.000
[doorbell rings]

225
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.000
Ramsbottom?

226
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.000
[snickers] Bottom.

227
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.000
I need a word with you both.
Sure, but what--

228
00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.000
I'm sorry.
There's no time for chitchat.

229
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Maxime Le Mal has sent you
a message from prison.

230
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.000
Bonjour, Gru.

231
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.000
I know you can hear me,
so hear this.

232
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.000
You think you can humiliate me
and get away with it? Yes?

233
00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.000
But, no!

234
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.000
When I break out of prison,
I'm coming for my revenge, Gru!

235
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:48.000
But this time,
I won't go so easy on you!
[laughs]

236
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.000
And I know where you live!

237
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:55.000
So you better sleep
with one eye open,
because you can't hide from me!

238
00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.000
Sweet dreams, Gru-ser!

239
00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.000
[both gasp]

240
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.000
Don't worry.
He can't get out of there.

241
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:04.000
It's a maximum security prison.

242
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.000
Ah, yes, well, um...
[clears throat]

243
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
...he escaped yesterday.

244
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.000
What?

245
00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.000
Leave our home?

246
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.000
Oh, no. You're gonna love it.

247
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.000
It's called "the safe house,"

248
00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.000
and it's fun, and it's safe,
and it's fantastic
and we're going.

249
00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.000
Yeah, you'll get a new room,
go to a new school.

250
00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.000
It'll be fun, right?

251
00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Everything's gonna be new.
We love new!

252
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.000
What about all my friends?

253
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.000
You'll make new friends.

254
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.000
Probably better ones.

255
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.000
[groans]

256
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.000
[muffled] I can't believe this.

257
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.000
Yes, yes. Lot of emotions.
Big life change.

258
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.000
Less talking, more walking.

259
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.000
Come on, here we go.

260
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.000
[Lucky bleats]

261
00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:52.000
[sniffles] I'm sorry
you can't go with us, Lucky.

262
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.000
[bleats]

263
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.000
Take good care of him.

264
00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.000
Be good, Lucky!

265
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:02.000
Don't forget
to practice your tricks!

266
00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.000
[sighs]

267
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.000
We'll arrive at
the AVL safe house
in a few hours.

268
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:11.000
Mayflower is a lovely town.

269
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.000
A lovely, safe, boring town.

270
00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.000
Trust me,
it is for the best, Gru.

271
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.000
And what about Grandma
and Uncle Dru?

272
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.000
I'm sorry. No one can know
of your whereabouts,
not even family.

273
00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.000
Bingo!
There's your silver lining.

274
00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:27.000
And you promise
to take care of
the other Minions?

275
00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:30.000
They'll be safe and sound
at AVL Headquarters.

276
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.000
I have big plans for them.

277
00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.000
[scoffs] Good luck with that.

278
00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.000
["BOOMBAYAH" playing]

279
00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:48.000
[Minions clamoring, laughing]

280
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:57.000
[grumbles] That is it!

281
00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.000
[tires screech]

282
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.000
[air brakes hiss]

283
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.000
Quiet!

284
00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:11.000
You are now on Carl's bus.

285
00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.000
And Carl is
a longtime AVL employee

286
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.000
whose retirement benefits
are almost vested.

287
00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:22.000
So, while on Carl's bus,
you follow Carl's rules.

288
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:27.000
No shenanigans,
no antics and no tomfoolery.

289
00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.000
Tom?
[blows raspberry]

290
00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.000
So this ends now.

291
00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:35.000
Or you're gonna see
a side of Carl
you do not wanna see.

292
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:38.000
Do I make myself clear? [grunts]

293
00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.000
[Minion] Bazooka!
[Minions laughing]

294
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.000
[party horns blaring]

295
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.000
[clamoring]
[Carl]
This won't st-- [groans]

296
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.000
Carl does not like this!

297
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.000
Watch your hands.
What are you doing?
Who's pinching?

298
00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.000
No, no!

299
00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:02.000
[Silas] Here we are.
The town of Mayflower.

300
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:06.000
This safe house has been used
to protect our agents
for decades now.

301
00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.000
Whoa, look at that place.

302
00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:11.000
[Lucy] Wow, look at these lawns.
The flowers.

303
00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:14.000
-[chuckling] Whoa! That is cool.
-Are we really gonna live here?

304
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.000
[gasps]
Look at that fountain.
Whoa!

305
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.000
[Edith] Awesome.

306
00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.000
[snoring]
[Edith] Ooh, ooh, ooh,
is that one ours?

307
00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.000
Hey, hey.

308
00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.000
[Edith] Whoa, look at that.
[Agnes] Ooh, that's pretty.

309
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.000
[Lucy] I could get used to this.

310
00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.000
[snorts]

311
00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.000
[both laugh]

312
00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:32.000
[Agnes] Ooh, it looks like
a princess lives there.

313
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.000
And here it is.

314
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:38.000
Your new home.

315
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.000
[bird squawks]

316
00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.000
Oh.

317
00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.000
Hmm, no fountain.

318
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:48.000
I'm sure
it's gonna be great.

319
00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.000
Come on.

320
00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:52.000
Silas says that there is
a pool in the back.

321
00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.000
That'll be fun, huh?

322
00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.000
Wow, it's so cold
and uninviting.
[Agnes giggles]

323
00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.000
But in a homey
kind of way.
What?

324
00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Yes, everything here
is AVL standard.

325
00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:14.000
What it lacks in comfort,
it more than makes up for
in functionality.

326
00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:18.000
There's even
a fully automated lockdown mode.

327
00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.000
Isn't that fun?

328
00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.000
Ooh, full lockdown mode.
[chuckles]

329
00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
Yay.

330
00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.000
[gasps]
It has a vending machine.
Oh! [chuckles]

331
00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.000
I love this place!

332
00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.000
Ooh. [speaks Minionese]

333
00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.000
[screams]

334
00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.000
[speaks Minionese]

335
00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.000
Eh, eh. [speaks Minionese]

336
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.000
[groaning]
[laughing]

337
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.000
This will be great.

338
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.000
All right,
now down to business.

339
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:45.000
For your own safety,
you'll all be assuming
new identities.

340
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:48.000
New identities?
Is that really necessary?

341
00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.000
It's not up for debate, Gru.

342
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.000
Now, you are
a solar panel salesman.

343
00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:56.000
Lucy, you're a hairstylist
at an upscale salon.

344
00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:00.000
A hairstylist? Yes, jackpot!

345
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.000
Silas, did you choose that
because you knew
I cut my own hair,

346
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.000
and that I would
totally rock at this?

347
00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.000
No.

348
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.000
"Chet Cunningham."

349
00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.000
Ah, that's got
a nice ring to it.

350
00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.000
Girls.

351
00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.000
Cool. I'm Blair.

352
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.000
"Britney"?

353
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.000
My name is Bree?

354
00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:21.000
Oh, come on.
There are worse names than Bree.

355
00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.000
Yeah, like Blanche.

356
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.000
[laughs] Yes, Margo.

357
00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:28.000
Blanche? Ugh,
that is a terrible name.
[laughs]

358
00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:30.000
Imagine being named Blanche.
[chuckles]

359
00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.000
Truly, I cannot think
of a worse--

360
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.000
My name's Blanche, isn't it?

361
00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.000
Yep.
[children giggle]

362
00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.000
Well, I'll get used to it.

363
00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:41.000
Well, why don't you girls go
and pick out your rooms

364
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:45.000
while I have a word
with your parents?
[speaking Minionese]

365
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.000
Yes, I didn't want
to frighten the girls,

366
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:52.000
but it is absolutely crucial
you keep your true identities
under wraps.

367
00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.000
Gru, you're going to have to try
to not be so "Gru-ish."

368
00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:58.000
What is that supposed to mean?

369
00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:02.000
Well, I'm just saying
you tend to stand out
in a crowd, that's all.

370
00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:06.000
You know... [stammers]
...like the way you're always
cranky and irritable.

371
00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:10.000
And how you make things
a bit awkward
for everyone around you.

372
00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.000
You do do that. [chuckles]
I mean, you know--

373
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.000
Okay, enough.

374
00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:17.000
I don't make people
awkward or uncomfortable.

375
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.000
I'm very comforting.

376
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.000
Like a nice meat loaf.

377
00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:23.000
I'm pretty delicious.

378
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:29.000
This is not awkward.
You're the ones
who are making it awkward.

379
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.000
Gru, you have to blend in.

380
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.000
Your family's lives
are at stake.

381
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.000
You understand?

382
00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.000
Of course, yes.
Fully understand.
[giggles]

383
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:40.000
We would do anything
to keep our family safe. Yeah.

384
00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:43.000
Right, well, I'll be in contact
when this is all over.

385
00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:49.000
Until then,
capturing Maxime Le Mal
is our top priority.

386
00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.000
Stay safe.

387
00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.000
[door closes]

388
00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:56.000
You know what, Gru,
maybe this isn't so bad.

389
00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:00.000
We need a break
from chasing down villains
and dangerous missions, right?

390
00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.000
We can actually be
a normal family for once.

391
00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:08.000
[gasps] And I can finally spend
some real bonding time
with the baby.

392
00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.000
It's gonna be great.
Right, pal?

393
00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.000
Who's got your nose?
Who's got--

394
00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.000
He's got my nose.
[gurgles]

395
00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:20.000
Quite the grip there.
That kid is strong.

396
00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.000
[groans]

397
00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.000
Ah.

398
00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.000
[humming]

399
00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.000
[babbles]

400
00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.000
[exclaims]

401
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.000
[shouting]

402
00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:45.000
[grunts]

403
00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.000
["Freedom" playing]

404
00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:50.000
♪ Let's be free, baby
And cruise the world ♪

405
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.000
♪ Are you with it, girl? ♪

406
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.000
♪ I'm free to do what I want ♪

407
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.000
♪ And have a good time ♪

408
00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.000
[laughing]

409
00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:01.000
Thank you.
Look at everyone. Yes.

410
00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.000
We are having
a good time, right?

411
00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:06.000
[singing]
♪ I'm free to do what I want ♪

412
00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.000
♪ And have a good time ♪

413
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.000
Whoo! Whoo! Whoo!

414
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.000
[cheering]
Whoo-hoo!

415
00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.000
[laughs]
No, I love you. [kisses]

416
00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.000
Thank you, my beautiful army.

417
00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:21.000
Maxime's back, baby. [laughs]

418
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:28.000
And a special merci beaucoup
to everyone who helped me
break out of AVL prison.

419
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.000
Todd and Linda, where are you?
Where are you? Yes.

420
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.000
For distracting the guards.

421
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:35.000
Oh, très magnifique.
Yeah!

422
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.000
Now, silence!

423
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:40.000
We must make Gru suffer
for arresting me.

424
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.000
[chuckles]

425
00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.000
And what better way

426
00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:46.000
than to take away from him
his precious little baby.

427
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:49.000
[cockroaches gasp]
I want to take that baby.
[laughs]

428
00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.000
Whoa.

429
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.000
[whistles]
Yeah!

430
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.000
Oh, Maxime.

431
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.000
No, no. Wait, wait. Not Maxime.

432
00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:59.000
What if I start going by
"Cockroach Man," huh?

433
00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:02.000
Little on the nose,
but it is very clear.

434
00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.000
It's good, no?
Ugh.

435
00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:08.000
I am not calling you
that stupid name,
but I love this evil plan.

436
00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.000
Well, Gru has it coming.

437
00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:13.000
He humiliated me
in front of the whole school.

438
00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.000
I had my trophy and everything.

439
00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.000
But now the game begins.
[cockroach babbles]

440
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:24.000
He runs and hides
like the mouse,
and we find him like the cat.

441
00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:27.000
Game on.

442
00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.000
[Ron giggling]

443
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.000
[speaking Minionese]
[giggles]

444
00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:35.000
-[speaking Minionese]
-[giggles]

445
00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.000
[screams]

446
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.000
[chuckles]

447
00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:44.000
Okay, we've got Chet's famous,
super cheesy scrambled eggs.

448
00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.000
And Blanche's famous bacon
that spells your name.

449
00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:51.000
-Here you go, Britney.
-[burbles]

450
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:55.000
Wait, I can't say
my name is Britney.

451
00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.000
That would be a lie.

452
00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Yes.

453
00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.000
But we aren't
"stupposed" to lie.

454
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.000
Don't think of it as lying.

455
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.000
Think of it
as high-stakes pretending.

456
00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Well, I'm not going to.

457
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:10.000
Bah, it's just
a little white lie.

458
00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.000
Agnes, as your father,

459
00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.000
I command you to lie.

460
00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:15.000
No.

461
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.000
-Yes, lie.
-Mm-mmm.

462
00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:19.000
You are walking
on thin ice, little lady.

463
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:21.000
Hmm!

464
00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.000
[exclaims, chews]

465
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:25.000
Why can't you be more
like your sister Edith?

466
00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:27.000
She lies all the time.

467
00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:28.000
No, I don't.

468
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:30.000
See? See? She's lying right now.

469
00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.000
Beautifully, I might add.

470
00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:33.000
[Lucy] Okay, you guys.

471
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:35.000
This is our first big day
in Mayflower,

472
00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.000
and I say
we make it a great one.

473
00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:39.000
Right, Chet Jr?
[giggles]

474
00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:42.000
Whoo-hoo, Mayflower. Yes!
Whoo-hoo. [chuckles]

475
00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:44.000
We're gonna be late for karate.

476
00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:46.000
And you have to
get Margo to school.
Ah.

477
00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.000
It's gonna be awesome.
Ugh. Yay.

478
00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.000
Hey, you just have to
put yourself out there,

479
00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:55.000
and I promise Mayflower
will love Chet Cunningham.

480
00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:58.000
Well, they're gonna love him
just as much as I do.

481
00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:02.000
And you, little man,
are gonna have so much fun
with your daddy today.

482
00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:03.000
[babbles]

483
00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:06.000
Yep, just you and Dada.

484
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:08.000
Come on, say it. Dada.

485
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:11.000
Dada.

486
00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:14.000
[blows raspberry]

487
00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:17.000
Gonna be a fun day.

488
00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:24.000
[breathes deeply]

489
00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.000
["Hot for Teacher" plays]
Hup, hup, hup!

490
00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.000
Hup, hup, hup, hup!

491
00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:35.000
Buddies.

492
00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:36.000
Okay.

493
00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:38.000
[speaks Minionese]

494
00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:41.000
[exclaims, giggles]

495
00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:43.000
Thanks a lot, guys.
Ah, ha-ha, buddy.

496
00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:46.000
[speaking Minionese]
...check ya.

497
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:48.000
[giggles]

498
00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:50.000
All right. Thanks, hon.

499
00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:52.000
Bye.
Bye.

500
00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:54.000
Look, Margo, neighbors.

501
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:56.000
Hello!

502
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.000
Hmm?

503
00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:58.000
Come on.

504
00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:00.000
You got this, Chet.

505
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.000
[groans]

506
00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:05.000
I'm your new neighbor,
Chet Cunningham.

507
00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:07.000
Uh-huh. Perry Prescott.

508
00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:11.000
So, what, uh, brings you
to the neighborhood, Chet?

509
00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.000
Well, uh...

510
00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:18.000
[gasps] Solar panels. That's it.
I sell solar panels.

511
00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:21.000
Have you joined
the solar revolution?

512
00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.000
Yeah, no.

513
00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:25.000
Uh, I think I'm good.

514
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:26.000
Good to know.

515
00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:28.000
So, what do you do, Perry?

516
00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.000
I own Prescott Motors.

517
00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:34.000
The largest auto dealer
in the state.

518
00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
Wow, that's impressive.

519
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:38.000
This is my daughter Margo.

520
00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:39.000
Bree, Dad.

521
00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:43.000
Ah, yes. Yes. Did I say "Margo"?

522
00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:45.000
It's funny,
because I was thinking--

523
00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:49.000
I was thinking about a fish
I once had as a pet,
named Margo.

524
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:54.000
Who lived in the pond
and then died.

525
00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:55.000
Uh.

526
00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:58.000
Anyway, I, uh--

527
00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:02.000
I'm about to take Bree
to school for her first day.

528
00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:05.000
Yeah, I was about to take Poppy
to school, so...

529
00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:07.000
Poppy. Hello, Poppy.

530
00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.000
That's a fun name to say.

531
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.000
You want to carpool with us?

532
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:13.000
No.

533
00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:15.000
You could be friends
with Bree.

534
00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:16.000
Right, Bree?

535
00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:19.000
You don't have any friends.

536
00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:21.000
[chuckles]

537
00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:24.000
Well, love to chitchat, Chet,
but she's got school,

538
00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:27.000
and I'm meeting some pals
over at the country club, so...

539
00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.000
Ooh, country club.
That sounds like a lot of fun.

540
00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:36.000
If I were ever invited
to a country club,
I am sure that I would love it.

541
00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:40.000
Yeah, well,
we really have to get going,
so nice meeting you, Chet.

542
00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:42.000
["I'm Too Sexy" plays on stereo]

543
00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:48.000
Okay, cool.
Any time you want to hang out,
just hit me up with a text.

544
00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:50.000
He's gonna text me.

545
00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:52.000
That was painful.

546
00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:58.000
You'll see. By lunchtime,

547
00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:02.000
you will have forgotten
all about
your old, lousy friends.

548
00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:05.000
Mmm, not so sure about that.

549
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:11.000
[students chattering, giggling]
Right? Oh, my gosh.

550
00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:13.000
Not my problem, bro.

551
00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:16.000
[sighs]
Hey, honey,
you got this.

552
00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:17.000
You're smart.

553
00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:19.000
You're funny.

554
00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:21.000
What's there
to worry about, right?

555
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:24.000
They're gonna love you.

556
00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:26.000
Thanks, Gru.

557
00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:30.000
[Gru] Bye-bye.

558
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.000
Oh, please let them love you.

559
00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:35.000
[sighs]

560
00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:37.000
Ooh!

561
00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:41.000
Hey, Poppy.

562
00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:46.000
Eh...

563
00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:47.000
[horn honks]
[screams]

564
00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:50.000
Come on. Hey. Move it!

565
00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:53.000
Sorry. My bad.
I'm going. All right.

566
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:55.000
I'm going.

567
00:26:57.000 --> 00:27:00.000
Ooh, glassos.

568
00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:03.000
-[shouts]
-[screams]

569
00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:04.000
[groans]

570
00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:07.000
[straining]
[barking]

571
00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:09.000
[whimpers]

572
00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:10.000
[chuckles, speaks Minionese]

573
00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.000
[leash snaps]
[screams]

574
00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:14.000
[barking]
No, no, no. Sit. Sit.

575
00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.000
No.

576
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:20.000
[speaks Minionese]

577
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:24.000
[screams, speaks Minionese]

578
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
[speaking Minionese, muffled]

579
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:27.000
All right, gentlemen.

580
00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:30.000
Fall in.

581
00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:33.000
Some of you may be wondering
why you're here.

582
00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:34.000
Uh, sí.

583
00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:36.000
As you may or may not know,

584
00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:38.000
I was recently
called out of retirement

585
00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:41.000
to head up the AVL's
new top-secret initiative

586
00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:44.000
to take down Maxime Le Mal.

587
00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:46.000
And that's where you come in.

588
00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:47.000
We need volunteers.

589
00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:49.000
Me! Me! Me!

590
00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.000
We are looking for
the strong, the mighty...

591
00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:53.000
Ooh. [groans]

592
00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:54.000
...the fearless.
Uh, nope.

593
00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:57.000
We need the best of the best.

594
00:27:57.000 --> 00:28:01.000
So, who's it going to be?
[chuckles]

595
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:05.000
Yes, nice work, gentlemen.

596
00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:06.000
[speaking Minionese]

597
00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:08.000
[laughing]

598
00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:12.000
The AVL is known for
cutting-edge weapons
and vehicles,

599
00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:15.000
but now we are developing
cutting-edge agents.

600
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:19.000
And I can think of
no better guinea pigs than you.

601
00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:20.000
Guinea pigs!
[cheering]

602
00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:22.000
[blows raspberry]

603
00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:25.000
You will be the first
to test our super serum.

604
00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:28.000
Designed to transform you
into elite agents

605
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:33.000
with powers and abilities
far beyond those of mortal men.

606
00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:36.000
Or you might just explode.

607
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:37.000
We don't really know.

608
00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:40.000
Eh? Huh? [shouts]

609
00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:43.000
[Minions screaming]
Oh, ah.

610
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:45.000
Hey.

611
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:51.000
[Minions struggling]

612
00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:55.000
[yodels, growls]

613
00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.000
[chuckles]

614
00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:07.000
[chews, crunches]

615
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:12.000
[speaking Minionese]
[metal clanging]

616
00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:14.000
[pops]

617
00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:16.000
[giggles]

618
00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:19.000
[growling]

619
00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:24.000
Ladies and gentlemen,
I give you the Mega Minions.

620
00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:27.000
[cheering]

621
00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:31.000
[bell rings]

622
00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:33.000
Cool.

623
00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:35.000
Aw, you guys look adorable.

624
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:37.000
And-- And really tough
and scary.

625
00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:41.000
I'll look even better
when I have a black belt.
Hi-yah!

626
00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:44.000
Ooh, ooh!
I'm gonna break a brick
with my head.

627
00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:47.000
That's the spirit. Oh!
[gong sounds]

628
00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:49.000
Oh, okay. Now, go have fun
while I'm at work.

629
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:53.000
Blair and Britney.
Right?
Mmm.

630
00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:54.000
We will.

631
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.000
Okay. Bye, Mom.

632
00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:58.000
[Lucy] Bye.

633
00:29:58.000 --> 00:29:59.000
Got ya.
[giggling]

634
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:01.000
Hi-yah!

635
00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:02.000
Circle up, people.

636
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:03.000
[students giggling]

637
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:05.000
[grunting]

638
00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:07.000
Show respect for your sensei.

639
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:10.000
[students]
Yes, Sensei O'Sullivan.

640
00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:13.000
Hai!

641
00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:19.000
You, Moscovitch,
didn't I tell you
to cut that hair?

642
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:21.000
You look like a sheepdog.

643
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:22.000
Sorry, Sensei.

644
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.000
[whimpers, giggles]

645
00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Now, we have
two new students today
ready to begin their journey--

646
00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:31.000
Hi-yah! To awesomeness.

647
00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:33.000
-You, tiny girl.
-[gasps]

648
00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:36.000
Step forward
and tell us your name.

649
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:37.000
Um...

650
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:40.000
It's Britney.

651
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:43.000
Uh, m-my name?

652
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:46.000
I can't.

653
00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:48.000
There's no "can't" in karate.

654
00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:51.000
Ten push-ups after class!

655
00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:53.000
Hey, that's not fair.

656
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:58.000
Huh! Ha! You better not be
talking back to your sensei.

657
00:30:58.000 --> 00:31:00.000
Hi-yah! [karate yell]

658
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:04.000
Now, are you ready
to tell us your name
and participate?

659
00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:05.000
Mmm.

660
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:07.000
I guess not.

661
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:11.000
Then why don't you go sit
in the corner of
disgrace and reflection

662
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:15.000
and think about
what kind of person
you wanna be?

663
00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:23.000
Now, am I gonna get
any trouble from you?

664
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.000
Yeah, probably.

665
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:27.000
Excuse me?
[bones pop]

666
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:29.000
If you think
I'm above fighting children,

667
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:32.000
you picked the wrong dojo.

668
00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:36.000
[grunting]

669
00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:38.000
Hi-yah, hi-yah, hi-yah!
Hi-yah!

670
00:31:38.000 --> 00:31:40.000
[karate yell]
Ha!

671
00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:44.000
[sobs, groans]

672
00:31:44.000 --> 00:31:47.000
[all gasp]

673
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:48.000
[children cheer] Yeah!

674
00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:51.000
That was for my sister.

675
00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:53.000
[O'Sullivan screams]

676
00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:57.000
You broke my pinkie toe.

677
00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:02.000
[chuckles]
That's gonna be
a lot of push-ups.

678
00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:05.000
[Lucy] Okay,
then put this over here,
then the hair gel.

679
00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:07.000
Hair spray.
Oh, uh,
Mrs. Cunningham?

680
00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:09.000
Oh! Uh, yeah. [stammers] Hi.

681
00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:12.000
I have to say,
this is quite a résumé.

682
00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:14.000
Well, what can I say?

683
00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:15.000
I'm good at what I do.
[chuckles]

684
00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:18.000
Well, you are
exactly what we need here.

685
00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:21.000
Lot of vain, demanding divas
in this town.

686
00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:24.000
[both chuckle]

687
00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:27.000
I have a hair emergency, people.

688
00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:28.000
Where's what's-her-name?

689
00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:30.000
Remy? Rhonda?

690
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:31.000
Oh, Melora, I'm so sorry.

691
00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:33.000
Rachel's on maternity leave.

692
00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:36.000
What? Oh, that is unacceptable.

693
00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:41.000
But you are in luck,
because Blanche here
is fantastic.

694
00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:44.000
Perfect. I'll be in my chair.

695
00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:46.000
Okay, kiddo, you're up.

696
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:47.000
[chuckles]

697
00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:49.000
["Dynamite" plays]

698
00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:54.000
So, Melora,
what are we thinking?

699
00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:57.000
What if we just wet the hair
and let it dry in the air?

700
00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:59.000
Let nature do its thang...
[chuckles] ...you know?

701
00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:02.000
No, no, no, no.
That style is dead to me.

702
00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:05.000
It's-It's time
for a whole new Melora.

703
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:07.000
I want this.

704
00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:09.000
Wow. [chuckles]

705
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:11.000
Wow. Um...

706
00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:15.000
Okay, let's start with color?

707
00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:18.000
Yes, color.
Because that's what
you start with.

708
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:22.000
Little of this.

709
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.000
Some of that.

710
00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:25.000
Ooh, that's pretty.

711
00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:27.000
This isn't so hard.

712
00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:29.000
[sizzling]

713
00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:31.000
Uh...

714
00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:37.000
What?

715
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:39.000
[sniffs] Should it be smoking?

716
00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:41.000
Yes. Uh-huh.

717
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:43.000
Smoking means it's working.

718
00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:46.000
[gasps]

719
00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:51.000
[shouts]

720
00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:52.000
[whimpers]
What's going on?

721
00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:55.000
Perfect. No one panic.

722
00:33:55.000 --> 00:33:57.000
Call 911.

723
00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:00.000
[fire alarm ringing]

724
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.000
Quickly, quickly.

725
00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:08.000
Oh... [chuckles]
...wonder where they're going.

726
00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:11.000
[Maxime laughing]

727
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:14.000
Voilà! My latest creation.

728
00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:18.000
All of my transformation powers
in a handheld design, huh?

729
00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:20.000
Ay! I love it.

730
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:23.000
Oh, and look at
the little antenna.
That's so cute.

731
00:34:23.000 --> 00:34:25.000
It's not supposed
to be cute. No.

732
00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:28.000
I'm going for intimidating.
Terrifying, even.

733
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:32.000
Now, all I have to do is find
that walking boiled potato,

734
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:35.000
and his baby is mine.
[laughs]

735
00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:37.000
Check this out.
[alarm beeps]

736
00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:42.000
Whoa!

737
00:34:42.000 --> 00:34:45.000
[barking]

738
00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:49.000
[cackles]

739
00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:55.000
No, I kid you not.
I'm being serious-- Whoa!

740
00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:58.000
Whoa!

741
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.000
[shutter clicks]

742
00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:11.000
[Maxime cackles]

743
00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:15.000
Oh, this is going to be so good.

744
00:35:23.000 --> 00:35:25.000
[sighs]

745
00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:29.000
-Okay, Daddy is
officially exhausted.
-[gurgles]

746
00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:31.000
I changed your diaper.

747
00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:35.000
I've got your bottle,
your Binky,
and here are your balloons.

748
00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:38.000
[giggles]
There you go.
You like those, right?

749
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:40.000
All right.
A little bit of me time.

750
00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:44.000
[breathes deeply, exhales]

751
00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:48.000
[balloon pops]
Ah!

752
00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:51.000
[groans]

753
00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:55.000
[grunts]

754
00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:03.000
[horn honks]
[shouts]

755
00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:04.000
[groans]

756
00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:07.000
[growls]

757
00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:10.000
[whines]

758
00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:13.000
[groans]

759
00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:17.000
Someone put a glitter bomb
in my locker. Ugh.

760
00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:20.000
Teenagers are the worst.

761
00:36:20.000 --> 00:36:23.000
Yeah. Babies are
no picnic either.

762
00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:26.000
[giggles]

763
00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:30.000
[balloon pops]
[Gru] Ah!

764
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:32.000
Junior!

765
00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:38.000
[Ralph snoring]

766
00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:46.000
[shushes, speaks Minionese]

767
00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:48.000
Ah, okay. Okay.
[grunts]

768
00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:52.000
-[shushes]
-Dua Lipa prosciutto.

769
00:36:52.000 --> 00:36:54.000
[thuds]
[exclaims]

770
00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:56.000
[laughing]

771
00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:57.000
[speaks Minionese]

772
00:36:57.000 --> 00:37:01.000
[speaks Minionese]
Fire in the bowl.

773
00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:02.000
[both laugh]

774
00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:05.000
Good night, Ralph.

775
00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:08.000
[scatting]

776
00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:10.000
♪ Taking out the trash
'Cause I'm an awesome dad ♪

777
00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:12.000
♪ And the baby
Finally went to sleep ♪

778
00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:16.000
[scatting, humming]

779
00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:17.000
[person] Hello, Gru.

780
00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:21.000
Hello. Hey! What the...

781
00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:25.000
Oh, hello, Poppy.
Did you say something?

782
00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:28.000
Wha-- Uh... [stammers]
...my name's Chet, by the way.

783
00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:30.000
Chet Cunningham.

784
00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:34.000
Gru? What does that even mean?
[chuckles]

785
00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:38.000
It means you're bad at lying.

786
00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:40.000
Hey. That's not nice.

787
00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:42.000
Ever hear of
respecting your elders?

788
00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:44.000
I don't respect boomers.

789
00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:46.000
I just mock them.

790
00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:50.000
Ah, ha, ha. Is that, like,
a joke you read on the Web?

791
00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:54.000
Wow. "The Web"? How old are you?

792
00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:57.000
Well, old enough to know
that you are a rotten little--
[grunts]

793
00:37:57.000 --> 00:37:59.000
Huh?

794
00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:01.000
You better watch yourself.

795
00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:03.000
[gasps] Ooh-hoo. Oof.

796
00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:05.000
You used to be a master villain.

797
00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:09.000
[scoffs] That's not me.
I don't even see a resemblance.

798
00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:15.000
Clearly, you have the wrong guy,
as I sell, mmm, solar panels.

799
00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:18.000
Oh, don't worry.
I'm not gonna expose you.

800
00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:20.000
Because you're gonna
help me pull a heist.

801
00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:22.000
We start planning tomorrow.

802
00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:25.000
You want to pull a heist?
[chuckles]

803
00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:27.000
Listen, kid,
I'm not going to--

804
00:38:27.000 --> 00:38:28.000
No. You listen, old man.

805
00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:31.000
Ow.
I own you.

806
00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:36.000
And I promise,
you do not want to cross me.

807
00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:38.000
Okay. [stammers] All right.

808
00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:41.000
But tomorrow is
not really good timing.

809
00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:42.000
Bummer for you.

810
00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:44.000
Because this is happening.

811
00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:50.000
Unless you want the whole world
to know exactly who you are...

812
00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:55.000
Gru.

813
00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:59.000
[gasps] She is terrifying.

814
00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:02.000
[hums]

815
00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:06.000
[exclaims, speaks Minionese]

816
00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:09.000
[Minions cheer]

817
00:39:09.000 --> 00:39:12.000
[speaking Minionese]

818
00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:14.000
Ow!
Ooh!

819
00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:16.000
Whoo-hoo-hoo!

820
00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:18.000
[speaking Minionese] ...five!

821
00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:20.000
[chuckles]

822
00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:23.000
[screams]

823
00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:25.000
Oh! [speaks Minionese]

824
00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:27.000
-[shutter clicks]
-[screams]

825
00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:29.000
[microwave pings]
Yay!

826
00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:30.000
Aw. [speaks Minionese]

827
00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.000
[Mega Mel] Hey, Jiminy!

828
00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:34.000
No problemo.

829
00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:35.000
[shouts]

830
00:39:35.000 --> 00:39:38.000
[screams]

831
00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:46.000
[screaming]

832
00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:49.000
Oh, phew. [speaks Minionese]

833
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:52.000
Oy.
[laughs]

834
00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:55.000
[growls]

835
00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:58.000
[speaking Minionese]

836
00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:02.000
All right, all right.
Settle down.

837
00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:04.000
Settle down!

838
00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:05.000
Thank you.

839
00:40:05.000 --> 00:40:08.000
It's time to get you out
for some real-world training.

840
00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:10.000
Liberty.

841
00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:12.000
And, if you do well out there,

842
00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:16.000
you'll be
the AVL's new secret weapon.

843
00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:21.000
Pomodoro!

844
00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:24.000
[Minion] Ouch.

845
00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:32.000
I'm quite sure
I won't regret this.

846
00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:34.000
No.
The painters canceled.
Uh-huh.

847
00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:36.000
True story.
Wow.

848
00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.000
I don't know
what is the deal with--

849
00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:39.000
[Gru] Morning, neighbors.

850
00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:40.000
Hey there!

851
00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:43.000
Still waiting on
that invite, Perry.

852
00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:44.000
Ugh.
Oh!

853
00:40:44.000 --> 00:40:47.000
No. No, no.
Yoo-hoo!

854
00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:48.000
Patsy!
[Patsy] Oh, neighbors.

855
00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:50.000
Oh, Patsy.

856
00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:52.000
Hi there.
I'm Perry's wife, Patsy.

857
00:40:52.000 --> 00:40:55.000
Oh! I'm Blanche.
And this is Chet.

858
00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:59.000
Hi. So, I look over here
and I see you...
[laughs]

859
00:40:59.000 --> 00:41:02.000
...and I have
one of my brilliant ideas.

860
00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:04.000
Perry needs a fourth
for tennis tomorrow.

861
00:41:04.000 --> 00:41:05.000
Oh, honey.

862
00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:07.000
[chuckles] I don't know.

863
00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:09.000
He doesn't seem like
much of a tennis guy.

864
00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:13.000
Much of a tennis guy?
I'm too much of a tennis guy.

865
00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:14.000
I'm Mr. Tennis.

866
00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:18.000
It's my favorite
of all the sports games.

867
00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:23.000
With the racket
and with the balls.
So yellow and fuzzy.

868
00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:24.000
[groans, grunts]

869
00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:25.000
Oh, then we're all set.

870
00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:28.000
See you two
at the club tomorrow.

871
00:41:28.000 --> 00:41:29.000
Toodle-oo!

872
00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:33.000
Okay. Toodle-oo
to you two too. [laughs]

873
00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:34.000
So, you-- you play tennis?

874
00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:37.000
Yes. Yes. I play tennis.

875
00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:40.000
I'm pretty fantastic actually.

876
00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:42.000
Well, at least
I was at summer camp.

877
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:45.000
Wow. That's great.
Here you go. [kisses]

878
00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:47.000
-Okay, bye.
-[fusses]

879
00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:50.000
Have fun!

880
00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:52.000
There you go.

881
00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:54.000
Okay.

882
00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:57.000
[grunts] Huh?
[giggles]

883
00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:05.000
What the...

884
00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:07.000
[exclaims]

885
00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:09.000
[groans]

886
00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:22.000
Gru.

887
00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:25.000
You can't hide from me, Gru.

888
00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:27.000
Ay! My back is killing me.

889
00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:29.000
How long is this gonna take?

890
00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:31.000
It will take
as long as it takes.

891
00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:35.000
Mark my words, Gru will not win.

892
00:42:35.000 --> 00:42:37.000
This won't be like
the ninth-grade talent show.

893
00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:40.000
Ay, again with this.

894
00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:42.000
Yes, again.
It was a pivotal moment.

895
00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:44.000
Why can't you indulge me?

896
00:42:44.000 --> 00:42:46.000
[groans]
[sighs]

897
00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:50.000
It was the night
of the big show.
[groans]

898
00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:52.000
[Maxime]
I had practiced for weeks,

899
00:42:52.000 --> 00:42:56.000
perfecting a number that would
blow my classmates away.

900
00:42:56.000 --> 00:42:58.000
♪ Karma, karma
Karma, karma chameleon ♪

901
00:42:58.000 --> 00:43:01.000
[Maxime] I was about
to go on when...

902
00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:05.000
What? Wh-- Oh!
...I heard it.

903
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:10.000
♪ Karma, karma
Karma, karma chameleon ♪

904
00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:14.000
There was that little jerk
doing my big number.

905
00:43:14.000 --> 00:43:17.000
[young Gru] ♪ You come and go ♪

906
00:43:17.000 --> 00:43:19.000
He ruined everything.

907
00:43:19.000 --> 00:43:22.000
I couldn't go on after him.
I would have looked like a fool.

908
00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:24.000
Like I was copying him.

909
00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:27.000
Maybe it was just a coincidence.

910
00:43:27.000 --> 00:43:29.000
That was a very popular song.

911
00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:31.000
Oh, no, no, no, no. He knew.

912
00:43:31.000 --> 00:43:33.000
He did it on purpose.

913
00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:36.000
He reveled in
humiliating me. Oh!
[alarm beeps]

914
00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:37.000
What now?

915
00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:39.000
[sighs] We're low on fuel.

916
00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:41.000
It's always something.

917
00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:44.000
Look, I can never focus
on just being evil. [groans]

918
00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:48.000
Okay. Pull over.

919
00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:55.000
[barking]

920
00:44:01.000 --> 00:44:03.000
[whimpers]

921
00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:10.000
[coughs]

922
00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:17.000
Okay, let's see.

923
00:44:17.000 --> 00:44:20.000
Regular unleaded. Oh.

924
00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:22.000
Wow. It is expensive, no?

925
00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:26.000
Okay. Insert card
and remove rapidly.
[card reader beeps]

926
00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:28.000
"Card not read"?

927
00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:31.000
-[beeps]
-Oh, come on.

928
00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:32.000
Did you pull it out rapidly?

929
00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:34.000
Yes. Yes. Very rapidly.

930
00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:36.000
[beeping]
Come--

931
00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:39.000
[grunting]

932
00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:42.000
[beeps]
[shouts]

933
00:44:42.000 --> 00:44:46.000
Ay, get me a slushy.
It's my cheat day.

934
00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:50.000
Hey, you. Your stupid machine
won't read my card.

935
00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:52.000
Did you remove it rapidly?

936
00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:54.000
Yes.
[sighs]

937
00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:58.000
Well, sometimes it's too rapid.
You should probably try again.

938
00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:01.000
[growls] I don't have
time for this.

939
00:45:01.000 --> 00:45:03.000
Okay. Whoa!

940
00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:07.000
I'm trying to
destroy my arch nemesis!

941
00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:10.000
Now, give me 900 gallons
on pump four, you idiot.

942
00:45:10.000 --> 00:45:13.000
Whoa! Please, don't hurt me.

943
00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:15.000
Oh, I'm not going to hurt you.

944
00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:16.000
[chuckles]

945
00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:18.000
Wha--

946
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:21.000
[exclaims]

947
00:45:23.000 --> 00:45:25.000
[muttering]

948
00:45:25.000 --> 00:45:27.000
Oh! Look at you!

949
00:45:27.000 --> 00:45:30.000
Ha, ha! Much better.

950
00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:32.000
Now, get me a purple slushy!

951
00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:34.000
[groans, growls]

952
00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:36.000
I'm not paying for that,
just so you know. So there.

953
00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:38.000
[chuckles] I know. I'm so bad.

954
00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:40.000
[laughs]
[mutters]

955
00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:43.000
[bell rings]

956
00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:48.000
Hmm. Okay, why don't you guys
pick out a healthy cereal?

957
00:45:48.000 --> 00:45:52.000
[gasps] This is
Lucky's favorite cereal.

958
00:45:52.000 --> 00:45:54.000
You don't think he'll forget me?

959
00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:55.000
Do you?

960
00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:58.000
Oh, sweetheart,
that's impossible.

961
00:45:58.000 --> 00:46:01.000
You play with Lucky
and dress him up.

962
00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:03.000
And you guys have your podcast.

963
00:46:03.000 --> 00:46:08.000
There is no way in this world
he could ever forget
his best friend.

964
00:46:08.000 --> 00:46:11.000
[giggles] Thanks, Mom.

965
00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:12.000
Oh, lookit!

966
00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:15.000
This one has extra marshmallows.

967
00:46:15.000 --> 00:46:17.000
Double-frosted choco clusters.

968
00:46:17.000 --> 00:46:20.000
[Agnes] Yeah.
Yeah.
Let's go with those.

969
00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:22.000
All right. What else do we need?

970
00:46:22.000 --> 00:46:23.000
[gasps]

971
00:46:23.000 --> 00:46:25.000
[gasps] Oh, no.

972
00:46:25.000 --> 00:46:29.000
Nobody see. Nobody notice.
Nobody notice.

973
00:46:29.000 --> 00:46:31.000
[Agnes exclaims]

974
00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:32.000
[exhales]

975
00:46:32.000 --> 00:46:34.000
[Edith] What's wrong?
Huh?

976
00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:36.000
Oh, nothing. Just, uh... Ooh.

977
00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:39.000
Stretching before
we hit the aisles.

978
00:46:39.000 --> 00:46:42.000
Shopping is the number one
cause of pulled hamstrings.

979
00:46:42.000 --> 00:46:45.000
Huh. You probably
didn't know that.
[laughs]

980
00:46:47.000 --> 00:46:48.000
Okay, all stretched. Let's go.

981
00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:51.000
Quickly. Quick, quick, quick.

982
00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:54.000
[sighs] Okay.
Coast is clear-- [screams]

983
00:46:56.000 --> 00:46:57.000
[grunts] Oh.

984
00:46:57.000 --> 00:47:00.000
[gasps] You.

985
00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:01.000
[chuckles]
[employee sighs]

986
00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:05.000
You did this to me, you fraud.

987
00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:06.000
Come on, girls.

988
00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:07.000
Clean up on aisle nine!

989
00:47:07.000 --> 00:47:11.000
I've always wanted to say that.
Just hide over here.

990
00:47:11.000 --> 00:47:13.000
What does that lady want?

991
00:47:13.000 --> 00:47:16.000
Lady? I didn't see a lady.

992
00:47:17.000 --> 00:47:19.000
[gasps] Lady!

993
00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:21.000
Come on. Let's go.

994
00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:22.000
Faster!
Whoa!

995
00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:24.000
You're no hairdresser.

996
00:47:24.000 --> 00:47:26.000
[Lucy whimpers]

997
00:47:26.000 --> 00:47:28.000
I'm on to you! Get back here.

998
00:47:28.000 --> 00:47:30.000
I gotta get out of here.

999
00:47:39.000 --> 00:47:42.000
-[screams]
-[shouts]

1000
00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:48.000
Okay.

1001
00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:50.000
[breathing heavily]

1002
00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:53.000
[screams]

1003
00:47:53.000 --> 00:47:55.000
[wails]

1004
00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:57.000
Come back here.

1005
00:47:57.000 --> 00:48:00.000
Whoa-ho-ho. [giggling]

1006
00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:04.000
Hey! No, no, no, no!

1007
00:48:05.000 --> 00:48:09.000
-You can't just--
-Open, open, open!

1008
00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:16.000
Whoa!

1009
00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:19.000
Let's go!

1010
00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:22.000
[Melora shrieks]

1011
00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:24.000
Stop! Come here, you!

1012
00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:26.000
[panting]

1013
00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:29.000
[sobbing]

1014
00:48:29.000 --> 00:48:32.000
Whew. That was a close one.

1015
00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:34.000
Always a fun time
when you go shopping with Mom.

1016
00:48:34.000 --> 00:48:38.000
-Yeah! I feel so alive!
-Best shopping trip ever!

1017
00:48:43.000 --> 00:48:45.000
[meows]

1018
00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:52.000
["Through the Fire and Flames"
plays]

1019
00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:54.000
[meowing]

1020
00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:10.000
[music stops]

1021
00:49:10.000 --> 00:49:12.000
[announcer on game] Perfecto.
[meows]

1022
00:49:12.000 --> 00:49:13.000
[Gru] Poppy!

1023
00:49:13.000 --> 00:49:16.000
[gasps]
Poppy!

1024
00:49:16.000 --> 00:49:18.000
[meows]

1025
00:49:19.000 --> 00:49:21.000
I don't see her, Junior.

1026
00:49:21.000 --> 00:49:22.000
Look up, genius.

1027
00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:25.000
Huh? [groans]
[Poppy] You're late.

1028
00:49:25.000 --> 00:49:27.000
How do I get up there?

1029
00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:29.000
Use the trampoline.

1030
00:49:29.000 --> 00:49:31.000
Huh?

1031
00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:35.000
[sighs]

1032
00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:38.000
Here we go.

1033
00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:39.000
[panting]

1034
00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:41.000
[grunting]

1035
00:49:41.000 --> 00:49:43.000
[Junior giggles]

1036
00:49:43.000 --> 00:49:46.000
[breathing heavily]

1037
00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:50.000
[groans]

